{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cfgmv4ANxYz1cs9F31575","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe new unit (exception + handler + YAML + function) mirrors the existing `InvalidTelephone*` / `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` pattern well — package placement, `ExceptionHandler` naming, reuse of `ProblemDetails.build`, and the `next: checkUnique` wiring are all idiomatic and consistent with the codebase. One structural issue, though:\n\n**Duplicated normalization rule (the core concept of the spec).** The canonical \"normalized telephone = strip every non-digit\" rule lives in `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` (`original.replaceAll(\"\\\\D\", \"\")`). `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique` re-implements that same rule inline for existing owners (`stored.replaceAll(\"\\\\D\", \"\")`). The spec is explicitly about *normalized* telephones, so this normalization is the one piece of logic that must stay identical across both call sites — yet there is now no single source of truth. A maintainer who changes the normalization rule in `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` (e.g. a different stripping scheme) would silently leave the uniqueness check comparing against the old scheme.\n\nActionable fix: extract the digit-stripping into one shared helper (e.g. a small `OwnerTelephone.normalize(String)` in the `function.owner` package) and have both `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` and `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique` call it. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` keeps its length check; both share the stripping definition.\n\nSecondary observation (optional, judgment call): on this same `POST /owners` endpoint, the sibling `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler` responds with the endpoint's `OwnerFieldErrors` contract, while this new handler returns a `ProblemDetail`. The 400-field-validation vs 409-conflict distinction makes `ProblemDetail` defensible, so this isn't blocking — but it's worth a conscious decision rather than an accidental divergence in how the same endpoint reports telephone-related failures."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":792,"cache_read_input_tokens":25782,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":792},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8126686a-b26d-446e-81ba-d7e9864f3e78","uuid":"b03783f5-e544-4f25-91b1-2e6c6cd24c8b","timestamp":"2026-10-04T07:07:59.521Z","request_id":"req_011Cfgmv3YBJcCQW5GwM2UwV"}
